  "body": "Automated worker task `task-20260805-161157-close-a-real-fabrication-loophole--not-a`. Risk tier: tier1.\n\nSuperboss review: The intent and most of the mechanics of this diff are sound (a real deterministic char cap on oversized evidence leaves, and a merge rule that now always preserves existing canonical_umr_id/status/all_umr_ids/pr_number/pr_repo/not_found instead of silently overwriting them), and the full 116-test suite passes; however, live reproduction of the new plan_for_ocid()/main() code path against a seeded row shows a confirmed severe regression: main()'s --apply call to upsert_ocid_canonical_registry() only passes canonical_umr_id/status/all_umr_ids/evidence/pr_number/pr_repo/duplicate_reason/not_found/audit_raw_output, never the plan's existing commit_sha/file_name/file_path/merge_status/evidence_summary -- so upsert's ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE unconditionally sets those five columns to their unpassed defaults (NULL) via excluded.*, silently wiping out the real per-OCID backfill data just landed in PR #64 (49/69 commit_sha, 23/69 file_path, 57/69 merge_status, 69/69 evidence_summary) for every one of the 69 existing rows the very next time --apply runs -- which this same PR's own PROGRESS.md lists as its next queued action. This is exactly the class of silent, live-data-destroying overwrite this task's own stated mission is to eliminate, it is not covered by any of the new or existing tests (none of which seed/assert on commit_sha/file_name/file_path/merge_status/evidence_summary through plan_for_ocid()->upsert), and it was independently reproduced live in this review (before/after row dump) rather than inferred from the diff alone. Separately, the PR's own new addendum doc ships with literal 'TBD' placeholders for its claimed live-apply results and PROGRESS.md's own Remaining section still lists the live re-run and independent review as outstanding, so this diff is not actually ready to represent itself as a completed, verified task even setting the bug aside.",
